 ## Background
-The method originates from the paper "GRF: Learning a General Radiance Field for 3D Representation and Rendering" [S1]. It was developed to address the sub-optimality of using raw RGB values directly, which are sensitive to environmental noise and lighting [S1]. The approach leverages an encoder-decoder CNN with skip connections and optional fully connected layers to learn general patterns for each pixel [S1].
+The method originates from the GRF (General Radiance Field) paper, which proposed using a CNN module to extract robust per-pixel features for 3D representation and rendering [S1]. It was developed to overcome the sub-optimality of using raw RGB values directly [S1]. The ResUNet variant was later introduced in PI-NeRF to provide a larger perceptual field for pose estimation and feature consistency [S2].
 
